  "description": "CR 712.11a, 715.3a, 715.2b, 715.4, 701.8a, 400.7, 603.6a: Dion, Bahamut's Dominant, tapping, exiles itself and returns transformed; Bahamut, Warden of Light enters with a lore counter, its chapters I and II put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature its controller controls and give them flying until end of turn, and chapter III destroys a target permanent and returns the card front face up as a new Dion, whose enters trigger makes a Knight",
  "note": "Turn 1: after the activation Bahamut has one lore counter; chapter I puts a +1/+1 counter on alice's Grizzly Bears and Knight Errant, not on Bahamut itself nor bob's Hill Giant, and the two fly that turn only. Turn 4: chapter II adds a second counter and flying again. Turn 7: chapter III destroys the Hill Giant, then Bahamut returns as Dion with no lore counters (not sacrificed by CR 715.4 while chapter III is on the stack), and the new Dion's enters trigger makes a Knight token. Turn 7's Bears flying 0 shows chapter II's grant ended. Knight Errant still flies then, from the new Dion's static.",
